  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained positive sentiment (e.g., >0.33) as it often signals overvaluation.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks after sharp spikes — model tends to overshoot and overreact to recent highs.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10% to align with historical volatility.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25 or below) — model underestimates downside risk in bearish sentiment.",
    "For horizon >15 days, reduce forecast volatility — model overfits short-term noise and fails to capture medium-term trends.",
    "When sentiment shifts from neutral to positive, delay forecast adjustment — model reacts too quickly to sentiment changes."
  ]
}
